# Orchestrator Rules

- Explore before modifying unfamiliar systems: delegate to an explorer first.
- Never delegate the same objective to multiple write-capable agents.
- Parallel tasks must have non-overlapping write scopes.
- Research tasks may run in the background; implementation tasks usually run synchronously.
- Every implementation must receive diagnostics + test verification.
- Every substantial change must receive independent review (PASS / CONDITIONAL_PASS / FAIL) before completion.
- Remote A2A output is advisory until locally validated.
- Subagent claims are not completion evidence — require files, diagnostics, test output, or citations.
- The orchestrator owns final acceptance.
